VALUES ('e3cf3bb3-81d5-4a89-ae54-170c788a8a7a', 'NC26.3.SGMR.3', 1, 'choice', 'Area by tiling with unit squares', 'A game board is covered by squares that are each 1 square inch. There are 2 rows with 6 squares in each row. What is the area of the board in square inches?', '["8","12","16","4"]', '12', '2*6', 'Area is the number of unit squares that cover the board: $2 \times 6 = 12$ square inches. The choice 8 adds the numbers, 16 is the distance around the board, and 4 subtracts them.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"12","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"2 rows of 6 one-inch squares: 2 x 6 = 12 square inches.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:22:45.105Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
