VALUES ('9e6021ae-a107-4cc5-8502-7dd3ddd497e1', 'NC26.4.ANR.7', 2, 'numeric', 'Features of a pattern', 'A pattern starts at 5 and follows the rule "add 5". How many of the first 12 numbers in the pattern end in the digit 0?', '[]', '6', '12/2', 'The numbers are 5, 10, 15, 20, ... up to 60. They end in 5 and 0 in turn, so half of the 12 numbers end in 0. That is 6 numbers.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"6","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"First 12: 5, 10, ..., 60. Ending in 0: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60 = 6.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:20:19.061Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
