VALUES ('e5698841-ef12-4ac6-8089-61d9d5ad20a9', 'NC26.4.ANR.7', 3, 'numeric', 'Growing shape pattern', 'The number of squares in a growing pattern is 7 in Figure 1, 12 in Figure 2 and 17 in Figure 3. The same number of squares is added each time. Which figure has 52 squares?', '[]', '10', '(52-7)/5+1', 'Each figure adds 5 squares. To get from 7 to 52 we need 45 more squares, which is 45 / 5 = 9 steps. 9 steps after Figure 1 is Figure 10.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"10","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Adds 5: 7, 12, 17, 22, 27, 32, 37, 42, 47, 52. 52 = 7 + 9x5, so Figure 10.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:20:19.061Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
