VALUES ('7a1b79fb-ef43-438b-abc7-c20da8271865', 'NC26.5.ANR.5', 3, 'numeric', 'Divide a whole number by a unit fraction', 'Rita has 3 ribbons that are each 5 feet long. She cuts all of them into pieces that are $\frac{1}{4}$ foot long. How many pieces does she cut?', '[]', '60', '3*5/(1/4)', 'The ribbons have $3 \times 5 = 15$ feet in all. Each foot makes 4 pieces, so there are $15 \times 4 = 60$ pieces.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"60","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Total length 3 × 5 = 15 feet. 15 ÷ 1/4 = 15 × 4 = 60 pieces (each 5-foot ribbon gives 20, × 3 = 60).","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T20:08:42.893Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
