VALUES ('60c32c93-6897-41e4-9146-2c4275f7d6e3', 'NC26.5.ANR.6', 1, 'choice', 'Describe the relationship between matching terms of two patterns', 'Pattern C is 3, 6, 9, 12. Pattern D is 9, 18, 27, 36. How is each number in D related to the matching number in C?', '["Each number in D is 3 times the matching number in C","Each number in D is 6 more than the matching number in C","Each number in D is 9 more than the matching number in C","Each number in D is 2 times the matching number in C"]', 'Each number in D is 3 times the matching number in C', NULL, 'Match them up: $3 \to 9$, $6 \to 18$, $9 \to 27$, $12 \to 36$. Each number is multiplied by 3. The differences (6, 12, 18, 24) keep changing, so it is not "more than".', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"Each number in D is 3 times the matching number in C","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"9 = 3 x 3, 18 = 3 x 6, 27 = 3 x 9, 36 = 3 x 12. 3 times. (Differences 6, 12, ... are not constant.)","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T20:08:42.947Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
