VALUES ('5473e33e-6c24-4325-91aa-5a98a1229d1f', 'NC26.5.ANR.6', 1, 'choice', 'Use the relationship between two patterns to find a term', 'Each number in Pattern Q is 4 more than the matching number in Pattern P. The 5th number in Pattern P is 15. What is the 5th number in Pattern Q?', '["11","60","19","20"]', '19', '15+4', 'The 5th number in Q is 4 more than the 5th number in P: $15 + 4 = 19$. The choice 11 subtracts, and 60 multiplies.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"19","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"5th in Q = 15 + 4 = 19.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T20:08:42.947Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
