VALUES ('5de822ab-5f6f-4675-9858-19b515d1180f', 'NC26.5.SGMR.2', 2, 'numeric', 'Read the coordinates of a point', 'Point A is at $(4, 6)$ and point B is at $(9, 2)$. How many units farther from the y-axis is B than A?', '[]', '5', '9-4', 'The distance from the y-axis is the x-coordinate. B is 9 units from it and A is 4 units, so B is 9 - 4 = 5 units farther.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"5","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Distance from the y-axis is the x-coordinate: B 9, A 4. 9 - 4 = 5.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T20:08:07.973Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
