VALUES ('7587982b-a54a-499b-933d-33c85da374e1', 'NC26.5.SGMR.4', 2, 'numeric', 'Volume from the area of the base and the height', 'A storage tank has a square base that measures 6 meters on each side. The tank is 4 meters tall. What is its volume, in cubic meters?', '[]', '144', '6*6*4', 'The base area is $6 \times 6 = 36$ square meters. Then $V = 36 \times 4 = 144$ cubic meters.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"144","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Base 6 x 6 = 36 sq m; 36 x 4 = 144 cubic m.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:22:28.485Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
