VALUES ('bf8d8d51-28d4-4384-b323-96573e8b4127', 'NC26.6.SGMR.2', 2, 'numeric', 'Reading ordered pairs and plotting by moves', 'Starting at the origin, a robot moves 6 units right, then 9 units down, then 6 units left. How many units is the robot from the origin when it stops?', '[]', '9', '9', 'After 6 right and 6 left the robot is back on the y-axis at x = 0. It is 9 units down, at $(0, -9)$, which is 9 units from the origin.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"9","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"(0,0) -> (6,0) -> (6,-9) -> (0,-9). Distance from origin along the y-axis: 9.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T20:19:32.493Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
