VALUES ('955c39c8-acbe-42f1-a656-dca1578c364e', 'NC26.M1.SGMR.1', 1, 'numeric', 'Use congruence to find lengths, angles and areas', 'In triangle $PQR$, $\angle P = 38^\circ$. The triangle is reflected across a line, and $P''$ is the image of $P$. What is the measure of $\angle P''$, in degrees?', '[]', '38', '38', 'A reflection is a rigid transformation, so it keeps angle measures. $\angle P''$ is also 38 degrees.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"38","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Reflection preserves angle measure: 38.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-18T01:07:47.267Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
